      "claim": "The intermediate range of the short‑run aggregate supply (AS) curve is upward‑sloping.",
      "evidence": "Standard macro‑economics textbooks (e.g., Mankiw, 9th ed., Ch. 23) divide the SRAS into three sections: horizontal (Keynesian), upward‑sloping (intermediate), and vertical (classical).",
      "weight": 0.3,
      "depends_on": []
    },
